  "mechanism": "Real editor scaling calls Component::setSize and setTransform. A synchronous parent childBoundsChanged callback can destroy the editor, after which the old applyUiScale continues to use openGLContext or the old timerCallback resumes touching destroyed controls. The same actual failure path was present in the unchanged 0.10.0 draft methods.",
  "correction": "Stack-owned Component::SafePointer checks follow setSize and setTransform before more member access. timerCallback also keeps its own stack SafePointer and returns after either applyUiScale call if a parent destroyed the editor.",
